(function(E){ const x = E["hr-m6"] = E["hr-m6"] || {units:{}}; x.units["hr-6-4"] = {"explain":{"id":"c-hr-6-4-e","course":"hr","unit":"hr-6-4","type":"explain","level":"B1","title":{"en":"Change and exits","tr":"Değişim ve ayrılışlar","fa":"تغییر و خروج از سازمان"},"objective":{"en":"After this lesson, you can announce a change clearly and run an exit interview with open questions.","tr":"Bu dersin sonunda bir değişikliği net biçimde duyurabilecek ve açık sorularla bir çıkış görüşmesi yapabileceksin.","fa":"بعد از این درس می‌توانی یک تغییر را روشن اعلام کنی و با سؤال‌های باز مصاحبه‌ی خروج انجام بدهی."},"hook":{"en":"Announce change clearly and ask leavers open questions. People judge a company by how it handles both. Arash heard about the move on WhatsApp. Leyla's next announcement says what will happen, and tells supervisors first.","tr":"Değişikliği net duyur, ayrılanlara açık uçlu sorular sor. İnsanlar bir şirketi bu ikisini nasıl yönettiğine bakarak değerlendirir. Arash taşınma haberini bir WhatsApp grubundan öğrendi. Leyla'nın bir sonraki duyurusu ne olacağını anlatıyor ve önce vardiya sorumlularına gidiyor.","fa":"تغییر را روشن اعلام کن و از کسانی که می‌روند سؤال باز بپرس. آدم‌ها شرکت را از روی رفتارش در این دو موقعیت می‌سنجند. آرش خبر جابه‌جایی را از یک گروه واتس‌اپ شنید. در اطلاعیه‌ی بعدی لیلا آمده که چه اتفاقی می‌افتد، و این بار اول سرپرست‌ها خبردار می‌شوند."},"before":{"en":"Announce a change to a team in three sentences: what changes, when, why and who to ask.","tr":"Bir değişikliği ekibe üç cümleyle duyur: ne değişiyor, ne zaman, neden ve kime sorulacak.","fa":"یک تغییر را در سه جمله به تیم اعلام کن: چه چیزی عوض می‌شود، کی، چرا و از چه کسی بپرسند."},"rounds":[[1,4],[2,3]],"stats":[{"label":{"en":"Key points","tr":"Ana nokta","fa":"نکته‌ی اصلی"},"value":"4"},{"label":{"en":"Key phrases","tr":"Anahtar ifade","fa":"عبارت کلیدی"},"value":"3"},{"label":{"en":"Practice tasks","tr":"Alıştırma","fa":"تمرین"},"value":"4"}],"points":[{"eyebrow":{"en":"The skill","tr":"Beceri","fa":"مهارت"},"head":{"en":"Say it clearly, ask it openly","tr":"Net söyle, açık sor","fa":"تغییر را روشن بگو، سؤال باز بپرس"},"body":{"en":"A change needs four facts: what, when, why and who to ask. Tell supervisors first, so staff get answers. With a leaver, use open questions: a yes or no teaches you nothing.","tr":"Bir değişiklik dört bilgi ister: ne, ne zaman, neden ve kime sorulacak. Çalışanlar cevap bulabilsin diye önce amirlere söyle. Ayrılan biriyle açık uçlu sorular kullan: evet ya da hayır sana bir şey öğretmez.","fa":"هر تغییر چهار نکته لازم دارد: چه، کی، چرا و از چه کسی بپرسند. اول به سرپرست‌ها بگو تا کارکنان بتوانند جواب بگیرند. با کسی که می‌رود، سؤال باز بپرس: از بله یا نه چیزی یاد نمی‌گیری."}},{"eyebrow":{"en":"The language","tr":"Dil","fa":"زبان"},"head":{"en":"Announcing change with the passive; open questions for exits","tr":"Değişikliği edilgen yapıyla duyurmak; ayrılış için açık sorular","fa":"اعلام تغییر با مجهول؛ سؤال‌های باز برای خروج"},"steps":[{"en":"Future change: will be + past participle.","tr":"Gelecekteki değişiklik: will be + past participle.","fa":"برای تغییر در آینده، will be و اسم مفعول می‌آید.","ex":"New shift times will be introduced on 1 September."},{"en":"Decision already made: has been + past participle.","tr":"Alınmış karar: has been + past participle.","fa":"برای تصمیمی که گرفته شده، has been و اسم مفعول می‌آید.","ex":"It has been decided to move the warehouse to Tuzla."},{"en":"Exit interviews: open questions with what, how, tell me about.","tr":"Çıkış görüşmeleri: what, how, tell me about ile açık sorular.","fa":"در مصاحبه‌ی خروج، سؤال‌های باز با what، how و tell me about بپرس.","ex":"What could we have done to keep you?"}],"table":{"headers":{"en":["Use","Example"],"tr":["Kullanım","Örnek"],"fa":["کاربرد","مثال"]},"rows":[["Future change (passive)","New shift times will be introduced on 1 September."],["Decision made (passive)","It has been decided to move the warehouse to Tuzla."],["Open exit question","What could we have done to keep you?"],["Closed question (avoid)","Did you like your team?"]]},"tip":{"en":"Turkish 'uygulamaya konulacak' and Persian 'ejra khahad shod' put the passive in one verb, so learners drop be or the -ed: 'will be introduce'. English needs will + be + past participle.","tr":"Türkçede 'yeni vardiya saatleri 1 Eylül'de uygulamaya konulacak' deriz. İngilizcede üç parça gerekir: will + be + past participle (will be introduced).","fa":"در فارسی می‌گوییم «ساعت‌های جدید شیفت از اول سپتامبر اجرا خواهد شد». انگلیسی سه بخش می‌خواهد: will، be و اسم مفعول (will be introduced)."},"wrong":"New shift times will be introduce on 1 May.","right":"New shift times will be introduced on 1 May."},{"eyebrow":{"en":"Key phrases","tr":"Anahtar ifadeler","fa":"عبارت‌های کلیدی"},"head":{"en":"Phrases for this task","tr":"Bu görev için ifadeler","fa":"عبارت‌های این کار"},"phrases":[{"phrase":"What you tell me stays confidential: we share themes, not names.","meaning":{"en":"Makes it safe to be honest, and promises only what HR can keep.","tr":"Dürüst olmayı güvenli kılar ve yalnızca İK'nın tutabileceği bir söz verir.","fa":"فضایی امن برای صادق بودن می‌سازد و فقط قولی می‌دهد که منابع انسانی می‌تواند پایش بماند."}},{"phrase":"What could we have done differently?","meaning":{"en":"Invites honest feedback.","tr":"Dürüst geri bildirim ister.","fa":"بازخورد صادقانه را دعوت می‌کند."}},{"phrase":"Tell me more about...","meaning":{"en":"Follows up a short answer.","tr":"Kısa bir cevabın devamını ister.","fa":"یک جواب کوتاه را دنبال می‌کند."}}]},{"eyebrow":{"en":"At work","tr":"İş yerinde","fa":"در محیط کار"},"head":{"en":"Leavers start with the polite answer","tr":"Ayrılanlar önce kibar cevabı verir","fa":"کسی که می‌رود، اول تعارف می‌کند"},"body":{"en":"Exit interviews are often run by HR, not by the leaver's manager, and the answers stay confidential. Many people avoid criticising an employer on the way out, so the first answer is often the polite one. In the UK and the EU, some changes, such as new shift patterns, may need staff consultation first.","tr":"Çıkış görüşmelerini çoğu zaman ayrılan kişinin yöneticisi değil İK yapar ve cevaplar gizli kalır. Birçok kişi ayrılırken işvereni eleştirmekten kaçınır; bu yüzden ilk cevap çoğu zaman kibar olanıdır. Birleşik Krallık’ta ve AB’de yeni vardiya düzeni gibi bazı değişiklikler önce çalışanlarla danışma gerektirebilir.","fa":"مصاحبه‌ی خروج را اغلب واحد منابع انسانی انجام می‌دهد، نه مدیر کسی که می‌رود، و جواب‌ها محرمانه می‌ماند. خیلی‌ها موقع رفتن از کارفرما انتقاد نمی‌کنند، برای همین جواب اول اغلب جواب مؤدبانه است. در بریتانیا و اتحادیه‌ی اروپا بعضی تغییرها، مثل الگوی تازه‌ی شیفت، ممکن است اول به نظرخواهی از کارکنان نیاز داشته باشد."}}],"example":{"eyebrow":{"en":"Worked example","tr":"Çözümlü örnek","fa":"مثال حل‌شده"},"head":{"en":"From weak to strong","tr":"Zayıftan güçlüye","fa":"از پیام مبهم تا اعلام روشن و سؤال باز"},"text":"Facts: From 1 May shifts start at 7:00, to avoid traffic. The person is leaving the company.","item":"Shifts are changing soon. Did you like it here?","why":{"en":"Weak: vague, and a closed question. Strong: clear facts and an open question.","tr":"Zayıf: belirsiz ve kapalı bir soru. Güçlü: net bilgiler ve açık uçlu bir soru.","fa":"نسخه‌ی اول مبهم است و سؤال بسته می‌پرسد. نسخه‌ی دوم واقعیت‌ها را روشن می‌گوید و سؤال باز می‌پرسد."},"answer":"From 1 May, shifts will start at 7:00, to avoid traffic. What would have made you stay?","cut":["soon","Did you like it here?"],"cutHint":{"en":"Tap the vague date and the question a leaver can answer with one word.","tr":"Belirsiz tarihe ve ayrılan birinin tek kelimeyle cevaplayabileceği soruya dokun.","fa":"روی تاریخ مبهم و سؤالی بزن که کسی که می‌رود با یک کلمه جوابش را می‌دهد."}},"quick":{"prompt":"A leaver gives a very polite reason in the exit interview. What should HR keep in mind?","options":["The first answer is often the polite one","Polite answers are always the true ones","The leaver’s manager should ask instead"],"correct":0,"why":{"en":"The first answer is often the polite one: many people avoid criticising an employer on the way out, so ask open questions and listen.","tr":"İlk cevap çoğu zaman kibar olandır: Birçok kişi ayrılırken işvereni eleştirmekten kaçınır; bu yüzden açık uçlu sorular sor ve dinle.","fa":"جواب اول اغلب همان جواب مؤدبانه است: خیلی‌ها موقع رفتن از انتقاد کردن از کارفرما دوری می‌کنند، پس سؤال باز بپرس و گوش بده."},"point":4},"remember":{"en":"Could the person answer your question with one word? Then make it open: start with what or how. Result of this lesson: you can announce a change and run an exit interview. You also have the announcement.","tr":"Kişi soruna tek kelimeyle cevap verebilir mi? O zaman soruyu aç: what ya da how ile başla. Bu dersin sonucu: bir değişikliği duyurabilir ve çıkış görüşmesi yapabilirsin; elinde de duyuru metni olur.","fa":"آیا آن فرد می‌تواند با یک کلمه جواب سؤالت را بدهد؟ پس سؤال را باز کن: با what یا how شروعش کن. حالا می‌توانی تغییری را اعلام کنی و مصاحبه‌ی خروج برگزار کنی. متن اعلام هم آماده است."},"b2Point":{"eyebrow":{"en":"B2 track","tr":"B2 yolu","fa":"مسیر B2"},"head":{"en":"It-clefts and softened questions: It was the way we..., What we'd like to understand is...","tr":"It-cleft ve yumuşatılmış sorular: It was the way we..., What we'd like to understand is...","fa":"it-cleft و سؤال‌های نرم‌شده"},"steps":[{"en":"Point at the real cause: It + be + focus + that...","tr":"Asıl nedeni göster: It + be + odak + that...","fa":"علت اصلی را این‌طور نشان بده: It و be، بعد نکته‌ی اصلی و بعد that.","ex":"It was the way we announced it that upset people."},{"en":"Ask gently: What we'd like to understand is...","tr":"Nazikçe sor: What we'd like to understand is...","fa":"با ملایمت بپرس: ⁨What we'd like to understand is...⁩","ex":"What we'd like to understand is why you decided to leave."},{"en":"that (not what) in an it-cleft; no it after a wh-clause.","tr":"it-cleft'te that (what değil); wh-yapısından sonra it yok.","fa":"در it-cleft از that استفاده کن نه what؛ بعد از بخش wh کلمه‌ی it نیاور.","ex":"It was the message that hurt."}],"table":{"headers":{"en":["Pattern","Example"],"tr":["Kalıp","Örnek"],"fa":["الگو","مثال"]},"rows":[["It + be + focus + that...","It was the way we announced it that upset people."],["What we'd like to understand is...","What we'd like to understand is why you decided to leave."],["What I'd really value is...","What I'd really value is your honest view."]]},"body":{"en":"B2 track: in the exit interview, ask one softened wh-cleft question, and summarise his main point with an it-cleft.","tr":"B2 yolu: çıkış görüşmesinde yumuşatılmış bir wh-cleft sorusu sor ve ana noktasını bir it-cleft ile özetle.","fa":"مسیر B2: در مصاحبه‌ی خروج یک سؤال با wh-cleft نرم‌شده بپرس و نکته‌ی اصلی حرف آرش را با یک it-cleft خلاصه کن."}}},"grammar":{"id":"c-hr-6-4-g","level":"B1","course":"hr","unit":"hr-6-4","title":"Announcing change with the passive; open questions for exits","titleTr":"Değişikliği edilgen yapıyla duyurmak; ayrılış için açık sorular","exp":{"en":"A change announcement focuses on what will happen, not on who decided it, so it often uses the passive: will be + past participle for the future (\"New shift times will be introduced on 1 September.\"), has been + past participle for a decision already made (\"It has been decided to move the warehouse to Tuzla.\"). Keep be and the past participle: not \"will introduce\" (that means the times introduce something) and not \"will be introduce\". In an exit interview, use open questions that start with what, how or tell me about: \"What did you enjoy most about working here?\", \"What could we have done to keep you?\" Closed questions (Did you...? Was it...?) get one-word answers.","tr":"Bir değişiklik duyurusu kimin karar verdiğine değil, ne olacağına odaklanır, bu yüzden çoğu zaman edilgen yapı kullanır: gelecek için will be + past participle (\"New shift times will be introduced on 1 September.\"), verilmiş bir karar için has been + past participle (\"It has been decided to move the warehouse to Tuzla.\"). Be'yi ve past participle'ı koru: \"will introduce\" değil (bu, saatlerin bir şeyi başlattığı anlamına gelir), \"will be introduce\" da değil. Çıkış görüşmesinde what, how ya da tell me about ile başlayan açık sorular kullan: \"What did you enjoy most about working here?\", \"What could we have done to keep you?\" Kapalı sorular (Did you...? Was it...?) tek kelimelik cevaplar getirir.","fa":"اطلاعیه‌ی تغییر روی «چه اتفاقی می‌افتد» تمرکز دارد، نه روی «چه کسی تصمیم گرفته»؛ برای همین اغلب مجهول است. برای آینده will be + اسم مفعول: «⁨New shift times will be introduced on 1 September.⁩» و برای تصمیمی که گرفته شده has been + اسم مفعول: «⁨It has been decided to move the warehouse to Tuzla.⁩» درست مثل «ساعت‌های جدید شیفت از اول سپتامبر اجرا خواهد شد» در اطلاعیه‌های فارسی. be و اسم مفعول هر دو لازم‌اند: «will introduce» یعنی خودِ ساعت‌ها چیزی را معرفی می‌کنند، و «will be introduce» هم غلط است. در مصاحبه‌ی خروج از سؤال‌های باز استفاده کن که با what، how یا tell me about شروع می‌شوند: «⁨What did you enjoy most about working here?⁩» و «⁨What could we have done to keep you?⁩» سؤال‌های بسته (Did you...? Was it...?) فقط جواب یک‌کلمه‌ای می‌گیرند."},"formsTable":{"headers":{"en":["Use","Example"],"tr":["Kullanım","Örnek"],"fa":["کاربرد","مثال"]},"rows":[["Future change (passive)","New shift times will be introduced on 1 September."],["Decision made (passive)","It has been decided to move the warehouse to Tuzla."],["Open exit question","What could we have done to keep you?"],["Closed question (avoid)","Did you like your team?"]]},"wrong":"New shift times will be introduce on 1 September.","right":"New shift times will be introduced on 1 September.","blank":{"sentence":"New shift times ___ on 1 September.","word":"will be introduced","distractors":["will introduce","will be introduce"]},"wrong2":"Did you like working here?","right2":"What did you enjoy most about working here?","blank2":{"sentence":"___ could we have done to keep you?","word":"What","distractors":["Did","How"]},"expParts":{"tryFrom":"blank","hook":{"en":"Arash heard about the move on WhatsApp. Leyla's next announcement says what will happen, and tells supervisors first.","tr":"Arash taşınma haberini bir WhatsApp grubundan öğrendi. Leyla'nın bir sonraki duyurusu ne olacağını anlatıyor ve önce vardiya sorumlularına gidiyor.","fa":"آرش خبر جابه‌جایی را از یک گروه واتس‌اپ شنید. در اطلاعیه‌ی بعدی لیلا آمده که چه اتفاقی می‌افتد، و این بار اول سرپرست‌ها خبردار می‌شوند."},"tryWhy":{"en":"will be introduced: the times do not introduce anything; they are introduced. Keep will + be + past participle.","tr":"will be introduced: saatler bir şey getirmez; onlar getirilir. will + be + past participle'ı koru.","fa":"جواب will be introduced است: ساعت‌ها چیزی را اجرا نمی‌کنند؛ اجرا می‌شوند. هر سه بخش will، be و اسم مفعول را نگه دار."},"rule":[{"en":"Future change: will be + past participle.","tr":"Gelecekteki değişiklik: will be + past participle.","fa":"برای تغییر در آینده، will be و اسم مفعول می‌آید.","ex":"New shift times will be introduced on 1 September."},{"en":"Decision already made: has been + past participle.","tr":"Alınmış karar: has been + past participle.","fa":"برای تصمیمی که گرفته شده، has been و اسم مفعول می‌آید.","ex":"It has been decided to move the warehouse to Tuzla."},{"en":"Exit interviews: open questions with what, how, tell me about.","tr":"Çıkış görüşmeleri: what, how, tell me about ile açık sorular.","fa":"در مصاحبه‌ی خروج، سؤال‌های باز با what، how و tell me about بپرس.","ex":"What could we have done to keep you?"}],"test":{"en":"Could the person answer your question with one word? Then make it open: start with what or how.","tr":"Kişi soruna tek kelimeyle cevap verebilir mi? O zaman soruyu aç: what ya da how ile başla.","fa":"آیا آن فرد می‌تواند با یک کلمه جواب سؤالت را بدهد؟ پس سؤال را باز کن: با what یا how شروعش کن."},"contrast":{"en":"Turkish 'uygulamaya konulacak' and Persian 'ejra khahad shod' put the passive in one verb, so learners drop be or the -ed: 'will be introduce'. English needs will + be + past participle.","tr":"Türkçede 'yeni vardiya saatleri 1 Eylül'de uygulamaya konulacak' deriz. İngilizcede üç parça gerekir: will + be + past participle (will be introduced).","fa":"در فارسی می‌گوییم «ساعت‌های جدید شیفت از اول سپتامبر اجرا خواهد شد». انگلیسی سه بخش می‌خواهد: will، be و اسم مفعول (will be introduced)."}},"errorWatch":[{"find":["will be introduce","will be use","will be hold","will be send","has been decide","it has decided to"],"fix":{"en":"Keep be + past participle: 'New shift times will be introduced', 'It has been decided'.","tr":"be + past participle'ı koru: 'New shift times will be introduced', 'It has been decided'.","fa":"be و اسم مفعول را نگه دار: «New shift times will be introduced» و «It has been decided»."}},{"find":["did you like working here","was it good working here","are you happy to leave"],"fix":{"en":"This is a closed question. Open it: 'What did you enjoy most about working here?'","tr":"Bu kapalı bir soru. Aç: 'What did you enjoy most about working here?'","fa":"این سؤال بسته است. بازش کن: «⁨What did you enjoy most about working here?⁩»"}}]},"b2":{"id":"c-hr-6-4-b2","level":"B2","track":"B2","course":"hr","unit":"hr-6-4","title":"It-clefts and softened questions: It was the way we..., What we'd like to understand is...","titleTr":"It-cleft ve yumuşatılmış sorular: It was the way we..., What we'd like to understand is...","exp":{"en":"Two focusing patterns help in exits and change. An it-cleft points at one thing as the real cause: \"It was the way we announced it that upset people, not the move.\" The pattern is It + be + the focus + that + the rest. A softened wh-cleft lets you ask a hard question gently: \"What we'd like to understand is why you decided to leave.\" It is much softer than the blunt \"Why are you leaving?\" Traps: use that, not what, in an it-cleft (\"It was the message what hurt\" is wrong), and do not add it after the wh-clause (\"What we'd like to understand it is\" is wrong).","tr":"İki odaklama kalıbı ayrılış ve değişim konuşmalarında yardımcı olur. It-cleft, gerçek sebep olarak tek bir şeyi işaret eder: \"It was the way we announced it that upset people, not the move.\" Kalıp: It + be + odak + that + geri kalan. Yumuşatılmış bir wh-cleft zor bir soruyu nazikçe sormanı sağlar: \"What we'd like to understand is why you decided to leave.\"; sert \"Why are you leaving?\" yerine. Tuzaklar: it-cleft'te what değil that kullan (\"It was the message what hurt\" yanlış) ve wh-yapısından sonra it ekleme (\"What we'd like to understand it is\" yanlış).","fa":"دو الگوی «برجسته‌سازی» در گفتگوهای خروج و تغییر به کارت می‌آید. it-cleft انگشت را روی یک چیز به‌عنوان علت اصلی می‌گذارد: «⁨It was the way we announced it that upset people, not the move.⁩» یعنی «چیزی که مردم را ناراحت کرد، شیوه‌ی اعلامش بود، نه خودِ جابه‌جایی». الگو: it + فعل be + نکته‌ی اصلی + that + بقیه‌ی جمله. wh-cleft نرم‌شده هم به تو اجازه می‌دهد یک سؤال سخت را با ملایمت بپرسی: «⁨What we'd like to understand is why you decided to leave.⁩»، به‌جای سؤال تند «⁨Why are you leaving?⁩». دو تله: در it-cleft از that استفاده کن نه what («It was the message what hurt» غلط است)، و بعد از بخش wh کلمه‌ی it اضافه نکن («What we'd like to understand it is» غلط است)."},"formsTable":{"headers":{"en":["Pattern","Example"],"tr":["Kalıp","Örnek"],"fa":["الگو","مثال"]},"rows":[["It + be + focus + that...","It was the way we announced it that upset people."],["What we'd like to understand is...","What we'd like to understand is why you decided to leave."],["What I'd really value is...","What I'd really value is your honest view."]]},"wrong":"It was the message what hurt, not the move.","right":"It was the message that hurt, not the move.","blank":{"sentence":"It was the way we announced it ___ upset people.","word":"that","distractors":["what","it"]},"wrong2":"What we would like to understand it is why you are leaving.","right2":"What we would like to understand is why you are leaving.","blank2":{"sentence":"___ was the WhatsApp message that hurt, not the move.","word":"It","distractors":["What","Who"]},"useIn":{"en":"B2 track: in the exit interview, ask one softened wh-cleft question, and summarise his main point with an it-cleft.","tr":"B2 yolu: çıkış görüşmesinde yumuşatılmış bir wh-cleft sorusu sor ve ana noktasını bir it-cleft ile özetle.","fa":"مسیر B2: در مصاحبه‌ی خروج یک سؤال با wh-cleft نرم‌شده بپرس و نکته‌ی اصلی حرف آرش را با یک it-cleft خلاصه کن."},"exitItem":{"from":"hr-6-4","kind":"blank","prompt":"It was the lack of training ___ made the change hard.","options":["what","that","it"],"correct":1,"why":{"en":"that: an it-cleft is 'It was ... that ...'. 'What' and 'it' don't link the two parts.","tr":"that: it-cleft yapısı 'It was ... that ...' şeklindedir. 'What' ve 'it' iki kısmı bağlamaz.","fa":"that درست است، چون ساختار It was ... that ... است. what و it دو بخش را به هم وصل نمی‌کنند."},"hint2":{"en":"It was ... ___ ... is a cleft sentence: it puts one thing in focus. Which word joins its two parts?","tr":"It was ... ___ ... tek bir şeyi öne çıkaran bir vurgu cümlesidir. İki kısmını hangi kelime bağlar?","fa":"⁨It was ... ___ ...⁩ جمله‌ای است که روی یک چیز تأکید می‌کند. کدام کلمه دو بخشش را به هم وصل می‌کند؟"}},"expParts":{"hook":{"en":"'It was the way we heard it that hurt, not the move.' Arash names the real cause.","tr":"'It was the way we heard it that hurt, not the move.' Arash tek bir kalıpla asıl nedeni gösteriyor.","fa":"«⁨It was the way we heard it that hurt, not the move.⁩» آرش با یک الگو علت اصلی را نشان می‌دهد."},"tryWhy":{"en":"It: an it-cleft starts with It + be. What would start a wh-cleft, which has no that.","tr":"It: it-cleft, It + be ile başlar. What ile başlayan wh-cleft olurdu ve onda that yoktur.","fa":"جواب It است: ساختار it-cleft با It و be شروع می‌شود. What یک wh-cleft می‌سازد که that ندارد."},"rule":[{"en":"Point at the real cause: It + be + focus + that...","tr":"Asıl nedeni göster: It + be + odak + that...","fa":"علت اصلی را این‌طور نشان بده: It و be، بعد نکته‌ی اصلی و بعد that.","ex":"It was the way we announced it that upset people."},{"en":"Ask gently: What we'd like to understand is...","tr":"Nazikçe sor: What we'd like to understand is...","fa":"با ملایمت بپرس: ⁨What we'd like to understand is...⁩","ex":"What we'd like to understand is why you decided to leave."},{"en":"that (not what) in an it-cleft; no it after a wh-clause.","tr":"it-cleft'te that (what değil); wh-yapısından sonra it yok.","fa":"در it-cleft از that استفاده کن نه what؛ بعد از بخش wh کلمه‌ی it نیاور.","ex":"It was the message that hurt."}],"test":{"en":"Remove 'It was' and 'that'. Is a normal sentence left (the message hurt)? Then the it-cleft is right.","tr":"'It was' ve 'that'i çıkar. Geriye normal bir cümle kalıyor mu (the message hurt)? O zaman it-cleft doğru.","fa":"«It was» و «that» را بردار. یک جمله‌ی عادی می‌ماند (the message hurt)؟ پس it-cleft درست است."},"contrast":{"en":"Persian 'in shive-ye e'lam bud ke narahat kard' and Turkish 'insanları üzen, duyuruluş şekliydi' use ke / -en, which learners translate as what. English it-clefts use that.","tr":"Türkçede 'İnsanları üzen, taşınma değil duyuruluş şekliydi' deriz. İngilizcede bu odak It + be + ... + that ile kurulur; that yerine what kullanılmaz.","fa":"در فارسی می‌گوییم «این شیوه‌ی اعلام بود که مردم را ناراحت کرد، نه خودِ جابه‌جایی». «که» را در این ساختار با that ترجمه کن، نه ⁨what⁩."}},"errorWatch":[{"find":["message what hurt","the move what","it was the way we announced it what","it was the message what","understand it is"],"fix":{"en":"Use that in an it-cleft and no it after a wh-clause: 'It was the message that hurt.' / 'What we'd like to understand is...'","tr":"it-cleft'te that kullan, wh-yapısından sonra it koyma: 'It was the message that hurt.' / 'What we'd like to understand is...'","fa":"در it-cleft از that استفاده کن و بعد از بخش wh کلمه‌ی it نگذار: «⁨It was the message that hurt.⁩» و «⁨What we'd like to understand is...⁩»"}}]},"vocab":{"id":"c-hr-6-4-v","level":"B1","category":"vocab","course":"hr","unit":"hr-6-4","goals":["career"],"title":{"en":"Change and Exits","tr":"Değişim ve Ayrılış","fa":"تغییر و خروج از سازمان"},"cards":[{"word":"announcement","sentence":"The announcement went out at nine.","meaning":{"en":"An official message that tells people news.","tr":"duyuru.","fa":"اطلاعیه؛ اعلام رسمی خبر"}},{"word":"consultation","sentence":"There will be a staff consultation before the move.","meaning":{"en":"Asking people for their views before deciding.","tr":"danışma, istişare.","fa":"نظرخواهی؛ مشورت با کارکنان پیش از تصمیم"}},{"word":"exit interview","sentence":"HR holds an exit interview on the last week.","meaning":{"en":"A meeting with someone who is leaving, to learn why.","tr":"çıkış görüşmesi.","fa":"مصاحبه‌ی خروج (گفتگو با کسی که از سازمان می‌رود، برای فهمیدن دلیلش)"}},{"word":"resign","sentence":"He resigned after twenty-three years.","gap":"resigned","accept":["resigned","resign"],"meaning":{"en":"To leave your job by choice.","tr":"istifa etmek.","fa":"استعفا دادن"}},{"word":"retire","sentence":"She plans to retire next year.","meaning":{"en":"To stop working because of age.","tr":"emekli olmak.","fa":"بازنشسته شدن"}},{"word":"site","sentence":"The new site is in Tuzla.","meaning":{"en":"A place where a building or work is.","tr":"tesis, saha.","fa":"محل کار؛ سایت"}},{"word":"rumour","sentence":"The rumour spread before the email.","meaning":{"en":"Information people pass on that may not be true.","tr":"söylenti.","fa":"شایعه"}},{"word":"transition","sentence":"The transition will take three months.","meaning":{"en":"The change from one situation to another.","tr":"geçiş.","fa":"دوره‌ی گذار"}},{"word":"farewell","sentence":"We had a farewell lunch for Arash.","meaning":{"en":"Saying goodbye, often with a small event.","tr":"veda.","fa":"خداحافظی؛ مراسم بدرقه"}},{"word":"confidential","sentence":"Your answers are confidential.","meaning":{"en":"Kept private; not shared.","tr":"gizli.","fa":"محرمانه"}}]},"story":{"id":"c-hr-6-4-s","level":"B1","genre":"Workplace","course":"hr","unit":"hr-6-4","title":{"en":"The Last Day","tr":"Son Gün","fa":"روز آخر"},"text":"The second forklift had arrived in March. Arash had sent Leyla a photo of it with one word: Finally.\n\nIn May, the board decided to move the Istanbul warehouse to a new site in Tuzla in September. New shift times would be introduced at the same time. For Arash, the new site meant ninety extra minutes on the road every day.\n\nHe resigned in June, after twenty-three years.\n\nOn his last Thursday, Leyla held his exit interview in the small room with the plant that nobody watered. \"Thank you for doing this,\" she said. \"What you tell me stays confidential: we share themes, not names. I want to understand what we could do better.\"\n\n\"It's the distance,\" Arash said. \"Ninety minutes. I'm not young.\"\n\nThat was true. But Leyla had a feeling it was not all. \"What else made the decision easier?\" she asked.\n\nHe looked at the plant for a while. \"I heard about the move from my driver's WhatsApp group. Two days before the email. Twenty-three years, and I learned it from a phone in the canteen.\"\n\nLeyla wrote it down exactly as he said it.\n\n\"What could we have done to keep you?\"\n\n\"Tell me first,\" Arash said. \"Tell all the supervisors first. Then the email. It was the way we heard it that hurt, not the move.\"\n\nThat evening Leyla wrote a draft for the next announcement, about the new shift times. It started with a meeting for supervisors, not with an email. It said what would change, when, why, and who to ask. And it said that a consultation would be held before anything was final.\n\nOn Friday there was a farewell lunch with grilled chicken. Deniz called from Dubai to say goodbye to the man he had never met but had heard about from everyone.","vocab":[{"word":"board","en":"The group of people who control a company.","tr":"yönetim kurulu","fa":"هیئت‌مدیره"},{"word":"canteen","en":"A place at work where people eat.","tr":"yemekhane","fa":"غذاخوری؛ سلف‌سرویس"},{"word":"supervisor","en":"A person who manages a team of workers.","tr":"vardiya sorumlusu, amir","fa":"سرپرست"},{"word":"draft","en":"A first version of a text.","tr":"taslak","fa":"پیش‌نویس"},{"word":"final","en":"Decided and not going to change.","tr":"kesin, nihai","fa":"نهایی؛ قطعی"}],"quiz":[{"prompt":"What hurt Arash most?","options":["The longer journey","Learning about the move from a WhatsApp group before the official email","The new forklift"],"correct":1},{"prompt":"Choose the correct sentence.","options":["New shift times will be introduced in September.","New shift times will introduced in September.","New shift times will be introduce in September."],"correct":0},{"prompt":"How did Leyla change the next announcement?","options":["She sent it by WhatsApp","Supervisors heard first, and a consultation was promised","She made it shorter"],"correct":1},{"prompt":"Why did Leyla ask \"What else made the decision easier?\"","options":["She felt distance was not the whole story","She wanted to end the interview","She did not believe him at all"],"correct":0}],"notice":{"en":"Arash gives one reason for leaving. Leyla thinks there is another. Watch the question that brings it out.","tr":"Arash ayrılmak için bir neden veriyor. Leyla başka bir neden daha olduğunu düşünüyor. Onu ortaya çıkaran soruya dikkat et.","fa":"آرش یک دلیل برای رفتن می‌گوید. لیلا فکر می‌کند دلیل دیگری هم هست. دقت کن کدام سؤال آن را بیرون می‌کشد."},"bridge":{"en":"'New shift times would be introduced...' and 'What could we have done to keep you?' Next: see the passive and open questions at work.","tr":"'New shift times would be introduced...' ve 'What could we have done to keep you?' Sırada: edilgen yapıyı ve açık soruları iş başında gör.","fa":"«⁨New shift times would be introduced...⁩» و «⁨What could we have done to keep you?⁩» قدم بعد: مجهول و سؤال‌های باز را در عمل ببین."}},"speaking":{"id":"hr-6-4","course":"hr","unit":"hr-6-4","topic":{"en":"Running an Exit Interview","tr":"Çıkış Görüşmesi Yapmak","fa":"انجام مصاحبه‌ی خروج"},"warmup":{"en":"Think of a job or place you left. What would you have told them if they had asked?","tr":"Ayrıldığın bir işi ya da yeri düşün. Sana sorsalardı onlara ne söylerdin?","fa":"کار یا جایی را به یاد بیاور که ترکش کردی. اگر از تو پرسیده بودند، چه می‌گفتی؟"},"questions":[{"en":"Open: thank Arash, explain the purpose and that his answers are confidential.","tr":"Aç: Arash'a teşekkür et, amacı ve cevaplarının gizli olduğunu açıkla.","fa":"گفتگو را شروع کن: از آرش تشکر کن، هدف مصاحبه را توضیح بده و بگو جواب‌هایش محرمانه می‌ماند."},{"en":"Ask three open questions: one with what, one with how, one with tell me about.","tr":"Üç açık soru sor: biri what, biri how, biri tell me about ile.","fa":"سه سؤال باز بپرس: یکی با what، یکی با how و یکی با tell me about."},{"en":"Summarise his main point and say what you will do with his feedback.","tr":"Ana noktasını özetle ve geri bildirimiyle ne yapacağını söyle.","fa":"نکته‌ی اصلی حرف‌هایش را خلاصه کن و بگو با بازخوردش چه خواهی کرد."}],"followups":[{"en":"Run the interview in 90 seconds, then 60, then 45.","tr":"Görüşmeyi 90, sonra 60, sonra 45 saniyede yap.","fa":"مصاحبه را یک بار در ۹۰ ثانیه، بعد در ۶۰ و بعد در ۴۵ ثانیه انجام بده."},{"en":"Arash gives a short answer: \"It's the distance.\" Ask one more open question to find out more.","tr":"Arash kısa bir cevap veriyor: \"Mesafe yüzünden.\" Daha fazlasını öğrenmek için bir açık soru daha sor.","fa":"آرش کوتاه جواب می‌دهد: «⁨It's the distance.⁩» یک سؤال باز دیگر بپرس تا بیشتر بفهمی."},{"en":"Now announce one real change at your workplace, using the passive once.","tr":"Şimdi iş yerindeki gerçek bir değişikliği, bir kez edilgen kullanarak duyur.","fa":"حالا یک تغییر واقعی در محل کارت را اعلام کن و یک بار از مجهول استفاده کن."}],"expressions":[{"phrase":"What you tell me stays confidential: we share themes, not names.","meaning":{"en":"Makes it safe to be honest, and promises only what HR can keep.","tr":"Dürüst olmayı güvenli kılar ve yalnızca İK'nın tutabileceği bir söz verir.","fa":"فضایی امن برای صادق بودن می‌سازد و فقط قولی می‌دهد که منابع انسانی می‌تواند پایش بماند."}},{"phrase":"What could we have done differently?","meaning":{"en":"Invites honest feedback.","tr":"Dürüst geri bildirim ister.","fa":"بازخورد صادقانه را دعوت می‌کند."}},{"phrase":"Tell me more about...","meaning":{"en":"Follows up a short answer.","tr":"Kısa bir cevabın devamını ister.","fa":"یک جواب کوتاه را دنبال می‌کند."}}],"culture":{"en":"In many companies, exit interviews are run by HR, not by the leaver's manager, and the answers are kept confidential. In many cultures people avoid criticising an employer on the way out, to protect references and relationships, so the first answer is often the polite one. In the UK and EU, some changes such as moving a workplace or changing shift patterns may require staff consultation first: check the local rules.","tr":"Birçok şirkette çıkış görüşmelerini ayrılan kişinin yöneticisi değil İK yapar ve cevaplar gizli tutulur. Birçok kültürde insanlar referanslarını ve ilişkilerini korumak için ayrılırken işvereni eleştirmekten kaçınır; bu yüzden ilk cevap çoğu zaman kibar olanıdır. Birleşik Krallık ve AB'de işyerini taşımak ya da vardiya düzenini değiştirmek gibi bazı değişiklikler önce çalışanlarla danışma gerektirebilir: yerel kuralları kontrol et.","fa":"در بسیاری از شرکت‌ها مصاحبه‌ی خروج را واحد منابع انسانی انجام می‌دهد، نه مدیر مستقیم فرد، و جواب‌ها محرمانه می‌ماند. در خیلی از فرهنگ‌ها آدم‌ها موقع رفتن از کارفرما انتقاد نمی‌کنند تا رابطه‌شان خراب نشود و بتوانند معرفی‌نامه بگیرند؛ برای همین جواب اول معمولاً جواب مؤدبانه است. در بریتانیا و اتحادیه‌ی اروپا، بعضی تغییرها، مثل جابه‌جا کردن محل کار یا تغییر الگوی شیفت‌ها، ممکن است قانوناً نیاز به نظرخواهی از کارکنان داشته باشد. قوانین محلی را بررسی کن."},"model":"Thank you for doing this, Arash. I want to learn what we could do better, and what you tell me stays confidential: we share themes, not names. What did you enjoy most about working here? You said it's the distance. What else made the decision easier? Tell me more about the WhatsApp message. What could we have done to keep you? Your main point: tell supervisors first. I'll share that with the board.","selfCheck":[{"en":"I explained the purpose and that his answers are confidential.","tr":"Amacı ve cevaplarının gizli olduğunu açıkladım.","fa":"هدف را توضیح دادم و گفتم جواب‌هایش محرمانه است."},{"en":"I asked open questions with what, how or tell me about.","tr":"what, how ya da tell me about ile açık sorular sordum.","fa":"با what، how یا tell me about سؤال‌های باز پرسیدم."},{"en":"After a short answer, I asked one more open question.","tr":"Kısa bir cevaptan sonra bir açık soru daha sordum.","fa":"بعد از یک جواب کوتاه، یک سؤال باز دیگر پرسیدم."},{"en":"I summarised his main point and said what I will do with it.","tr":"Ana noktasını özetledim ve bununla ne yapacağımı söyledim.","fa":"نکته‌ی اصلی‌اش را خلاصه کردم و گفتم با آن چه خواهم کرد."}]},"writing":{"id":"c-hr-6-4-w","title":{"en":"The shift-change announcement","tr":"Vardiya değişikliği duyurusu","fa":"اطلاعیه‌ی تغییر شیفت"},"course":"hr","unit":"hr-6-4","type":"writing","difficulty":"hard","prompt":{"en":"Write the announcement of the new shift times to the Istanbul team (70-100 words), sent after the supervisors' meeting: what will change, when, why, the consultation, and who to ask. Use the passive at least twice.","tr":"Vardiya sorumluları toplantısından sonra gönderilen, İstanbul ekibine yeni vardiya saatlerinin duyurusunu yaz (70-100 kelime): ne değişecek, ne zaman, neden, danışma süreci ve kime sorulacak. En az iki kez edilgen yapı kullan.","fa":"اطلاعیه‌ی ساعت‌های جدید شیفت را برای تیم استانبول بنویس (۷۰ تا ۱۰۰ کلمه)؛ اطلاعیه‌ای که بعد از جلسه با سرپرست‌ها فرستاده می‌شود: چه چیزی تغییر می‌کند، از کی، چرا، روند نظرخواهی و برای سؤال به چه کسی مراجعه کنند. دست‌کم دو بار از ساختار مجهول استفاده کن."},"model":"Dear all, As your supervisors explained on Monday, new shift times will be introduced when we move to the Tuzla site on 1 September. Two shifts will be used instead of three: 6:00 to 14:00 and 14:00 to 22:00. This change has been planned to reduce night driving and to match our clients' delivery times. Before anything is final, a consultation will be held on 15 July, and your views will be shared with the board. If you have questions, please speak to your supervisor or to me. Kind regards, Leyla Karimi, HR","frame":"Dear all, As your supervisors explained on ___, ___ will be introduced ___. ___ will be used instead of ___. This change has been planned to ___. Before anything is final, a consultation will be held on ___. If you have questions, please ___. Kind regards, ___","words":[{"word":"will be"},{"word":"consultation"},{"word":"questions"}],"minWords":70,"minSentences":6,"rubric":["Task done: what, when, why, consultation, who to ask","Organised: change first, reason, process, contact","Language: will be / has been + past participle used correctly","Tone: respectful and clear; people hear it from supervisors first"],"rubricI18n":{"tr":["Görev: ne, ne zaman, neden, görüş alma süreci, kime sorulacağı","Düzen: önce değişiklik, sonra sebep, süreç, iletişim kişisi","Dil: will be / has been + past participle doğru kullanılmış","Üslup: saygılı ve net; çalışanlar önce amirlerinden duyar"],"fa":["کامل بودن کار: چه چیزی، کی، چرا، نظرخواهی از کارکنان، از چه کسی بپرسند","نظم: اول تغییر، بعد دلیل، روند، فرد رابط","زبان: کاربرد درست will be / has been با اسم مفعول","لحن: محترمانه و روشن؛ کارکنان خبر را اول از سرپرستشان می‌شنوند"]},"portfolio":null,"parts":[{"t":{"en":"What will change","tr":"Ne değişecek","fa":"چه چیزی عوض می‌شود"},"find":["will be introduced","will be used","instead of"],"sample":"two shifts instead of three"},{"t":{"en":"When","tr":"Ne zaman","fa":"کی"},"find":["on 1 september","september","when we move"],"sample":"from 1 September, at the Tuzla site"},{"t":{"en":"Why","tr":"Neden","fa":"چرا"},"find":["to reduce","to match","has been planned"],"sample":"less night driving; match the clients’ delivery times"},{"t":{"en":"The consultation","tr":"Çalışanlara danışma","fa":"نظرخواهی از کارمندان"},"find":["consultation"],"sample":"a consultation on 15 July"},{"t":{"en":"Who to ask","tr":"Kime sorulacağı","fa":"از چه کسی بپرسند"},"find":["speak to your supervisor","questions"],"sample":"your supervisor or me"}]},"perspective":{"id":"c-hr-6-4-p","title":{"en":"Arash's last evening","tr":"Arash'ın son akşamı","fa":"آخرین شب آرش"},"course":"hr","unit":"hr-6-4","type":"perspective","minSentences":3,"prompt":{"en":"You are Arash on your last evening at Atlas. Write a journal entry of 3-4 sentences in first person: what will you miss, what do you wish had been different, and what do you want the young HR woman to remember?","tr":"Atlas'taki son akşamındaki Arash'sın. Birinci tekil şahısla 3-4 cümlelik bir günlük yaz: neyi özleyeceksin, keşke neyin farklı olmasını isterdin ve genç İK çalışanının neyi hatırlamasını istiyorsun?","fa":"تو آرش هستی، در آخرین عصرِ کارت در Atlas. از زبان خودت یادداشتی سه‌چهار جمله‌ای در دفترچه‌ات بنویس: دلت برای چه چیزی تنگ می‌شود، ای کاش چه چیزی جور دیگری بود و دوست داری آن کارشناس جوان منابع انسانی چه چیزی را همیشه به خاطر داشته باشد؟"}},"exit":{"id":"c-hr-6-4-x","course":"hr","unit":"hr-6-4","type":"exit","items":[{"from":"hr-6-4","kind":"blank","prompt":"New uniforms ___ in October.","options":["will be given out","will give out","will be give out"],"correct":0,"point":2,"why":{"en":"will be given out: the uniforms receive the action, so will be + past participle. 'Will give out' says the uniforms give something, and 'will be give out' drops the participle.","tr":"will be given out: üniformalar eylemi alır, bu yüzden will be + üçüncü hâl. 'Will give out' üniformaların bir şey dağıttığını söyler; 'will be give out' üçüncü hâli düşürür.","fa":"will be given out درست است، چون لباس‌ها توزیع می‌شوند و will be و اسم مفعول لازم است. will give out یعنی خود لباس‌ها چیزی پخش می‌کنند و will be give out اسم مفعول ندارد."}},{"from":"hr-6-4","kind":"blank","prompt":"___ did you enjoy most about working here?","options":["What","Did","How"],"correct":0,"point":2,"why":{"en":"What: an open question asks for an answer in the person's own words. 'Did' and 'How' don't fit 'did you enjoy most'.","tr":"What: açık uçlu soru kişinin kendi sözleriyle cevap ister. 'Did' ve 'How' 'did you enjoy most' ile uymaz.","fa":"What درست است، چون سؤال باز جواب را با حرف خود آدم می‌خواهد. Did و How با did you enjoy most جور نیستند."},"hint2":{"en":"An open question cannot be answered with yes or no. Which word asks for a thing?","tr":"Açık uçlu bir soru evet ya da hayırla cevaplanamaz. Hangi kelime bir şeyi sorar?","fa":"سؤال باز را نمی‌شود با بله یا نه جواب داد. کدام کلمه درباره‌ی یک چیز می‌پرسد؟"}},{"from":"hr-6-4","kind":"mcq","prompt":"Which exit-interview question is open?","options":["Did you like your team?","Was it the distance?","What did you enjoy most about working here?"],"correct":2,"point":2,"why":{"en":"'What did you enjoy most about working here?' is open: it can't be answered with yes or no. The other two invite only yes or no.","tr":"'What did you enjoy most about working here?' açık uçludur: evet ya da hayırla cevaplanamaz. Diğer ikisi yalnızca evet ya da hayır cevabına davet eder.","fa":"«What did you enjoy most about working here?» باز است و با بله یا نه جواب داده نمی‌شود. دو سؤال دیگر فقط بله یا نه می‌خواهند."}},{"from":"hr-6-3","kind":"blank","prompt":"Late deliveries ___ from 9% to 3%.","options":["felt","fell","falled"],"correct":1,"point":2,"why":{"en":"fell: the past of 'fall' is fell. 'Felt' is the past of feel, and 'falled' is not a word.","tr":"fell: 'fall' fiilinin geçmişi fell'dir. 'Felt' feel'in geçmişidir; 'falled' diye bir kelime yoktur.","fa":"fell درست است، چون گذشته‌ی fall همان fell است. felt گذشته‌ی feel است و falled وجود ندارد."}},{"from":"hr-6-1","kind":"blank","prompt":"Insurance covers 80 ___ of the cost.","options":["percents","per cent","percentage"],"correct":1,"point":2,"why":{"en":"per cent: a number + per cent, with no -s. 'Percents' is not used this way, and 'percentage' needs 'a ... of'.","tr":"per cent: sayı + per cent; -s almaz. 'Percents' bu şekilde kullanılmaz; 'percentage' 'a ... of' ister.","fa":"⁨per cent⁩ درست است: عدد و ⁨per cent⁩، بدون ⁨-s⁩. ⁨percents⁩ این‌طور به کار نمی‌رود و ⁨percentage⁩ به ⁨a ... of⁩ نیاز دارد."},"hint2":{"en":"After a number, English uses a fixed two-word form with no -s. Which option is that?","tr":"Bir sayıdan sonra İngilizce, sonunda -s olmayan iki kelimelik kalıp bir biçim kullanır. Hangi seçenek bu?","fa":"بعد از عدد، انگلیسی یک شکل ثابت دوکلمه‌ای بدون ⁨-s⁩ به کار می‌برد. کدام گزینه همین است؟"}},{"from":"hr-3-3","kind":"blank","prompt":"He ___ me he had worked here for 23 years.","options":["said","told","spoke"],"correct":1,"point":2,"why":{"en":"told: 'tell' takes a person (told me). 'Said' takes no person, and 'spoke' doesn't report words this way.","tr":"told: 'tell' bir kişi alır (told me). 'Said' kişi almaz; 'spoke' sözleri bu şekilde aktarmaz.","fa":"told درست است، چون tell شخص می‌خواهد (told me). بعد از said شخص نمی‌آید و spoke حرف را این‌طور نقل نمی‌کند."}},{"from":"hr-6-4","kind":"mcq","prompt":"Who should hear about a shift change first?","options":["The supervisors, so they can answer staff questions","The clients","Every driver, by group text"],"correct":0,"why":{"en":"The supervisors first: then staff get answers from the people they ask every day.","tr":"Önce vardiya amirleri: Böylece çalışanlar her gün soru sordukları kişilerden cevap alır.","fa":"اول سرپرست‌ها: این‌طوری کارمندها جوابشان را از همان کسانی می‌گیرند که هر روز از آن‌ها سؤال می‌کنند."},"point":1}]}}; })(globalThis.COURSE_FILES = globalThis.COURSE_FILES || {});
